LUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1`; a guard against accidental model use, not a security boundary) and which no model-facing skill or tool description mentions; the begin route and `BeginTurnAsync` keep today's behavior; AC-006 `SessionLogTurnEntity.IngressNonce` (string 64, nullable) with a unique filtered index on (WorkspaceId, SessionLogId, IngressNonce) where not null and a second unique filtered index on (WorkspaceId, RequestId) where IngressNonce is not null (minted ids are workspace-unique across sessions; legacy rows are untouched), added by migration `<utc>_AddSessionLogTurnIngressNonce` for SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server; a mint whose nonce exists returns the stored turn's requestId (a violation of the nonce index re-reads the owning turn and returns its requestId as `merged`; a violation of the requestId index generates a new requestId and retries at most 5 times after the original attempt (6 attempts in all), then fails with 500 `mint_collision_exhausted` (C9 ACKed by Codex at 2026-10-09T23:22:30Z); any other database error fails the mint). [A1]",
